[12.587809, "o", "--- ROUTE ---\r\n"]
[12.588999, "o", "Pipeline modules live with the CLI under /app/deskbin and as sibling sources under /app. Spool bytes sit in /app/dropwell. Fixture copies sit at /app/seed/dropwell. Side listing helper is /app/dropwalk.\r\n"]
[12.589214, "o", "--- FORMAT ---\r\n"]
[12.590067, "o", "CLAT dump (little-endian):\r\n\r\n  magic     4 bytes  \"CLAT\"\r\n  version   u16\r\n  write_stamp u32   dump-write unix seconds\r\n  nstreams  u16\r\n  then n directory entries: stype u32, rva u32, size u32\r\n\r\nStream type 3 (exception): dwLowDateTime u32, dwHighDateTime u32, code u32.\r\nThose two dwords are a Windows FILETIME (100-nanosecond ticks; 10000000 ticks per second).\r\nThe FILETIME epoch is 1601-01-01, 11644473600 seconds before Unix epoch.\r\n\r\nStream type 15 (misc): 16-byte guid, then companion u8 (0 = primary, 1 = extra).\r\n\r\nDigest on the keg is SHA-256 (sha256) of the dump file, written as lowercase hex.\r\n\r\nSequence uses these dump fields even when last-good is not present.\r\n\r\nExtra dumps added under the well, including names such as mid.clat, use this same layout.\r\nFixture copies of the well live at /app/seed/dropwell.\r\n\r\nKeg upload.json shape: {\"batch_count\":N,\"entries\":[{\"seq\":1,\"name\":\"<file>\",\"digest\":\"<hex>\",\"guid\":\"<hex>\"}]} with seq beginning at 1. batch_count is how many groups of three entries the upload splits into (the last group may be shorter). batch.tsv header is seq\tname\tdigest\tguid then matching rows. Success writes /app/kegbay/MARK as ok. Empty well, or /app/bin/clatter pour /app/scratch outside /app/dropwell, exits nonzero. On those failures /app/kegbay/MARK must not exist; a false body is not the failure signal.\r\n"]
[12.590245, "o", "--- TREE ---\r\n"]
[12.592698, "o", "/app/bin/clatter\r\n/app/deskbin/emit.rs\r\n/app/deskbin/main.rs\r\n/app/deskbin/parse.rs\r\n/app/deskbin/pipe.rs\r\n/app/deskbin/sum.rs\r\n/app/deskbin/usage.txt\r\n/app/dropwalk/mtime.rs\r\n/app/dropwell/a.clat\r\n/app/dropwell/a2.clat\r\n/app/dropwell/b.clat\r\n/app/dropwell/d.clat\r\n/app/dropwell/e.clat\r\n/app/dropwell/e2.clat\r\n"]
[12.59286, "o", "/app/dropwell/old.clat\r\n/app/fat.sh\r\n/app/fold.rs\r\n/app/kegbay/MARK\r\n/app/kegbay/batch.tsv\r\n/app/kegbay/pairs.tmp\r\n/app/kegbay/ribbon.txt\r\n/app/kegbay/upload.json\r\n/app/opsheet/FORMAT.txt\r\n/app/opsheet/MTIME_NOTE.txt\r\n/app/opsheet/ROUTE.txt\r\n/app/seed/dropwell/a.clat\r\n/app/seed/dropwell/a2.clat\r\n/app/seed/dropwell/b.clat\r\n/app/seed/dropwell/d.clat\r\n/app/seed/dropwell/e.clat\r\n/app/seed/dropwell/e2.clat\r\n/app/seed/dropwell/old.clat\r\n/app/stamp.rs\r\n/app/tidearc/README.txt\r\n/app/tidearc/lastgood.rec\r\n/app/walk.rs\r\n"]
[12.593106, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@45d1eb709689:/app# "]
[13.088886, "i", "printf '%s\\n' '--- ELF ---'; file /app/bin/clatter; printf '%s\\n' '--- BUILD/SOURCES ---'; find /app -maxdepth 3 -type f \\( -name 'Makefile' -o -name '*.c' -o -name '*.h' -o -name '*.cc' -o -name '*.cpp' -o -name '*.rs' \\) -print -exec sed -n '1,240p' {} \\;; printf '%s\\n' '--- LASTGOOD ---'; test -f /app/tidearc/lastgood.rec && cat /app/tidearc/lastgood.rec || true; printf '%s\\n' '--- CURRENT KEG ---'; for f in /app/kegbay/upload.json /app/kegbay/batch.tsv /app/kegbay/MARK; do echo \"[$f]\"; test -e \"$f\" && cat \"$f\" || echo MISSING; done\n"]
[13.090305, "o", "printf '%s\\n' '--- ELF ---'; file /app/bin/clatter; printf '%s\\n' '--- BUILD/SOURCES ---'; find /app -maxdepth 3 -type f \\( -name 'Makefile' -o -name '*.c' -o -name '*.h' -o -name '*.cc' -o -name '*.cpp' -o -name '*.rs' \\) -print -exec sed -n '1,240p' {} \\;; printf '%s\\n' '--- LASTGOOD ---'; test -f /app/tidearc/lastgood.rec && cat /app/tidearc/lastgood.rec || true; printf '%s\\n' '--- CURRENT KEG ---'; for f in /app/kegbay/upload.json /app/kegbay/batch.tsv /app/kegbay/MARK; do echo \"[$f]\"; test -e \"$f\" && cat \"$f\" || echo MISSING; done\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
